z5f = z3x (the incumbent) + SYM_RELAY with the hook before report() (z5e had it after). z5e's first mechanism games
(~/diag26b/sy, araid FreeTheCheese A and B) replayed z3x's attacker and rat masks r1-400 exactly: away from the kings
report() gossips an unreported mine almost every turn (GOSSIP_ALWAYS), so z5e's squeak was the turn's second and the
engine refused it. Here the relay squeaks first, every SYM_GOSSIP_EVERY (3) rounds while the rat's mask is sharper
than the shared one, an ally is within d2 16 and no seen cat can hear; report()'s squeak that turn is refused (no
side effects in z3x: BURN, KING_PRESS, TRAP_SHARE and TRIP_HALF are off), so a mine's gossip waits a turn. The merge
of heard SQ_SYM masks and the ledger hook (K 18) are z5e's. Evidence: bots/z5e/SNAPSHOT (rushers resolve the
symmetry hundreds of rounds before the king on FreeTheCheese, rift and clockwisdom, and never come home to tell it).
On FreeTheCheese the ROT and HOR enemy spots are adjacent ((29,3), (30,3)), so the rushers' target barely depends on
it there; rift (HOR and VER spots 51 tiles from the true one) and clockwisdom (dirt corners) are the cases that
matter.

